aka
===

This project is a Go rewrite inspired by portless
(https://github.com/vercel-labs/portless), Copyright Vercel Labs, licensed
under the Apache License, Version 2.0. A copy of that license is in
third_party/portless/LICENSE.

The following parts are translated from, or closely follow, portless's
TypeScript sources (packages/portless/src):

  - internal/ports: the app port range (4000-4999), random-then-sequential
    free port search, the per-address bind probe (127.0.0.1, ::1, 0.0.0.0,
    ::), and the browser "bad ports" skip list (from cli-utils.ts
    findFreePort / BLOCKED_PORTS).
  - internal/proxy: Host-header routing, the hop-count loop detection header
    and its threshold of 5, HTML-or-JSON error responses chosen by Accept,
    the X-Forwarded-* headers, and rewriting upstream redirects back to the
    public origin (from proxy.ts, including rewriteUpstreamLocation).
  - internal/runner: the child environment (PORT, HOST=127.0.0.1, a
    <TOOL>_URL variable), prepending node_modules/.bin to PATH, running the
    child in its own session and forwarding signals to its process group
    (from cli.ts and cli-utils.ts spawnCommand / killTree).
  - Test cases in internal/proxy and internal/detect port edge cases from
    proxy.test.ts and cli-utils.test.ts.

Listener detection, stdout URL scanning, the daemon protocol and the
connection-scoped route ownership are new in this project.
